From d87fd7ff941f076b0026de6847cf22cd62f2193d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Josh (via Claude)" <josh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 03:59:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Redesign nav, positions, transactions, and contributions

- Nav: horizontal top bar instead of a left sidebar
- Open Positions: single top-level tab with US / SG / HK sub-tabs
  (previously US was separate but SG+HK were combined)
- Transactions: add inline edit (PATCH) alongside delete; edits are
  re-validated against the full ledger (not just the edited row) so an
  edited Buy can't silently push a later Sell negative
- Portfolio %: no longer colored green / no leading '+' (it's a share
  of total, not a gain/loss figure) - applied to both the Open
  Positions 'Portfolio %' column and the Contributions '% of
  portfolio' column
- Open Positions: per-row Unrealized P/L (native currency) is now
  colored green/red like every other P/L figure in the app
- Contributions: 'Contribution history' is now a horizontal pivot
  (one row per month/label, one column per stakeholder, with row and
  column totals) instead of a flat ledger, matching how the sheet
  showed bulk monthly contributions
